 nav='<a href="#status">Launch status</a><a href="#squad">Squads</a><a href="#friends">Play with friends</a><a href="/#more-games">More games</a>'
 sections=[
 ('status','Warhammer Survivors co-op: the launch answer',f'''<p><strong>Plan for one human player.</strong> Auroch Digital's {ext(FAQ,'official FAQ')} says the launch focuses on single-player and that the community will be told if multiplayer is added. That covers both offline and online co-op: there is no announced launch option for a second person on the couch or across the internet.</p><p>The {ext(STORE,'Steam listing')} also identifies Single-player. As checked on 7 November 2026, the full game is still scheduled for 10 November; the available demo is not proof of a later multiplayer mode. A future possibility is not a confirmed release plan.</p><p>If playing together is essential, do not buy two copies or a console online subscription specifically for Warhammer Survivors co-op. Neither supplies the missing game mode.</p>'''),
 ('squad','Several characters on screen do not mean several players',f'''<p>Warhammer's squad system adds followers to a solo run. The developer's {ext(SQUAD,'Squad System announcement')} describes Keywords that determine who can wield a weapon: a weapon your champion cannot use can bring a follower who uses it for you. Those allies are part of your loadout, rather than a friend joining with another controller.</p><figure><a href="/assets/warhammer-survivors/squad-1280.webp"><img src="/assets/warhammer-survivors/squad-800.webp" srcset="/assets/warhammer-survivors/squad-800.webp 800w, /assets/warhammer-survivors/squad-1280.webp 1280w" sizes="(max-width:800px) calc(100vw - 40px), 800px" width="1920" height="1080" alt="A Warhammer Survivors champion and armed allies beside a tank, surrounded by Tyranids" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Official Steam gameplay image, © Games Workshop Limited. Several allies are visible; this is not evidence of multiplayer. Capture build unspecified; checked 7 November 2026.</figcaption></figure><p>Use the distinction when reading trailers or looking for a join button: <strong>a larger squad changes the solo build; it does not change the human player count.</strong> We have not tested a full run or a multiplayer workaround.</p>'''),
 ('friends','Choose a workable plan for your group',f'''<p>If your goal is a survivors run with friends, Vampire Survivors is a separate game with documented co-op modes. Its partnership with Warhammer does not transfer those modes to Warhammer Survivors. Use your devices to choose the next step:</p><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Group play choices; scroll horizontally"><table><thead><tr><th>Your group</th><th>Practical route</th><th>Check before starting</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Want Warhammer heroes specifically</td><td>Play individual Warhammer Survivors runs or take turns</td><td>Taking turns remains a solo session; no simultaneous friends mode is announced.</td></tr><tr><td>Two to four people at one screen</td><td>Vampire Survivors local co-op</td><td>Each player needs an input device. Multiple people cannot share one keyboard.</td></tr><tr><td>Friends on separate PCs or consoles</td><td>Vampire Survivors online co-op, after checking the platform pair</td><td>Each person needs a device and copy; different platform ecosystems are not universally compatible.</td></tr><tr><td>Mobile players</td><td>Vampire Survivors local co-op on one device with additional controllers</td><td>Landscape mode required; the online FAQ excludes mobile at online launch.</td></tr><tr><td>Two local players plus a remote friend</td><td>Re-plan the devices before choosing online</td><td>Vampire Survivors cannot mix couch and online modes in one session.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>These choices combine the two developers' rules; they are not our performance tests. For Vampire Survivors local requirements, use {ext(LOCAL,"poncle's local co-op FAQ")}. For online copies, subscriptions, mixed-mode restrictions and platform compatibility, use {ext(ONLINE,"poncle's online FAQ")}. The older local FAQ's online answer predates the separate online FAQ.</p><p>For the exact platform pairing and setup, continue to our <a href="/vampire-survivors/co-op/">Vampire Survivors co-op compatibility guide</a>. For example, Steam and Xbox are not one ecosystem merely because both can run on a PC; Xbox and the Microsoft Store/Game Pass PC version are the documented pair.</p>'''),
 ('save','Keep multiplayer and save transfer separate',f'''<p>Being able to move a save does not let two people share a run. Likewise, Steam Cloud on the product listing is not a promise of cross-platform progression. Do not assume that buying a console or mobile copy will preserve your PC unlocks.</p><p>Auroch's {ext('https://steamcommunity.com/app/3669620/announcements/','6 October release announcement')} explicitly says the earlier demo does not transfer progress to the updated demo, and demo progress does not carry into the full game. If your only reason for grinding now is to enter launch with completed unlocks, that effort will not accomplish it. Use the demo to judge whether you enjoy the solo loop instead.</p>'''),
 ('next','Before you invite anyone',f'''<ol><li>Decide whether Warhammer characters or simultaneous group play is your priority.</li><li>For Warhammer, plan separate solo sessions. Recheck the {ext(FAQ,'developer FAQ')} if a later update announces multiplayer.</li><li>For Vampire Survivors, write down each person's store/platform and whether they share a screen; check those against the <a href="/vampire-survivors/co-op/">co-op compatibility guide</a> before buying extra copies.</li></ol><p>Warhammer Survivors is a standalone Auroch Digital game, not a Vampire Survivors DLC. We do not provide an unofficial network patch or claim a working co-op mod.</p>''')]
 body=''.join(f'<section id="{i}"><h2>{h}</h2>{t}</section>'for i,h,t in sections)
 title='Warhammer Survivors Co-op: Solo Status & Friends Options'
 desc='Warhammer Survivors launches as single-player. Separate squads from co-op and choose a workable survivors game for local, online or mobile friends.'
